      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. Single doses are usually 500\u20131,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** The ordered amount is about twice the maximum daily dose. That raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n1700 mg may be a typo or a total-daily-dose mix-up. Possible intended orders include:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO two or three times daily\n- 1,700 mg total per day, divided, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was confirmed."
      }
     ],
